cff-version: 1.2.0
version: 4.0.0
message: "If you use this software or the derived data, please cite it as below."
title: "TCCounts: enumerating the specification space of western North Pacific and Philippine Area of Responsibility tropical cyclone count trends"
abstract: >-
  Recomputes tropical cyclone counts from the IBTrACS v04r01 western North
  Pacific archive for the basin and for the PAGASA Philippine Area of
  Responsibility hexagon, and fits a linear trend under every combination of
  six grading requirements, three intensity thresholds, four counting rules
  and fifty start years, and for three further series, 10,000 specifications
  in all. It
  decomposes the trend by storm class, dates changes in the record with step
  models, calibrates the significance test against fitted noise models, tests
  the specification curve as a whole, and compares the archive with PAGASA's
  own record of storms entering the PAR. Automated checks reproduce every
  reported value.
